## Edit a component on the host

Stop its container, then run it on the host on the same port (`mise run infra` starts the infrastructure alone):

{{if .Web}}    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Web}}
    mise run {{.DevWebTask}}

Editing {{.Backend}} runs the console on the host too (nginx in the container reaches only the {{.Backend}} container); run each task in its own terminal:

    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Backend}} {{.Web}}
    mise run {{.DevSrvTask}}
    mise run {{.DevWebTask}}

Once per clone: `npm --prefix {{.Web}} ci`.
{{else}}    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Backend}}
    mise run {{.DevSrvTask}}
{{end}}
